 {'id':'KY-VF62-06','severity':'high','obligations':['REPEATING_ROWS','ROUTE_OPTIONS'],'finding':'The exact route includes same-case dismissed or amended companion charges, but the builder requires a single classification for every charge and never collects/uses a charge-specific disposition or disposition date. Pure probes pass an explicitly dismissed or amended companion through validateKy; the actual scheduleSections function then describes it as convicted on the global record date. A mixed misdemeanor/violation case instead fails CHARGE_AND_RECORD_CLASSIFICATION_CONFLICT. The six retained fixtures are homogeneous and do not expose these failures.','currentArtifactDefect':False,'scope':'Directly measured current-builder/source-contract defect, not a claim that any retained fixture contains an undisclosed dismissed charge.','evidence':[legal+':186',legal+':325',memo+':273',builder+':169',builder+':423',E+'/source-contract-measurements.json#cases',E+'/source-contract-measurements.json#scheduleFunctionSource'],'consequentialLegalAmbiguity':'The held review expressly leaves unresolved how clerks handle dismissed/amended charges on the 2016 AOC form. Independent acceptance cannot silently settle that issue.','repairRequirement':'Preserve each charge’s actual classification/disposition/date, and safely stop or explicitly hand off the unresolved companion-charge treatment until the exact form handling is decided. Do not silently relabel a dismissed/amended charge as convicted or claim complete route coverage from homogeneous fixtures.'},
 {'id':'KY-VF62-07','severity':'medium','obligations':['ROUTE_OPTIONS'],'finding':'validateKy rejects every participant mailing state except KENTUCKY, even when the held source dropdown expressly permits the exact value Ohio and the case remains a Fayette County Kentucky case. The exact route restricts offense jurisdiction to Kentucky; it does not declare a Kentucky-residence requirement.','currentArtifactDefect':False,'scope':'Current builder limitation independently reproduced; all retained fixtures happen to have Kentucky addresses.','evidence':[builder+':160',legal+':197',E+'/current-evidence-measurements.json#sources[].fields[Def.Address.State]',E+'/source-contract-measurements.json#cases'],'repairRequirement':'Use the held source’s valid mailing-state options, preserving the Kentucky case/venue restriction separately.'},
 {'id':'KY-VF62-08','severity':'low','blocking':False,'obligations':['COMPONENT_SET'],'finding':'The conditional continuation schedule is appended to every current packet even when no text used fallback and only one charge exists. The petitionUsedFallback comparison treats the selected checkbox’s undefined completeValue as unequal to true. Thus the canonical schedule is caused by the checkbox, not overflow. The extra schedule accurately repeats current facts and does not itself invalidate filing.','currentArtifactDefect':True,'evidence':[builder+':504',E+'/source-contract-measurements.json#unconditionalScheduleTrigger'],'repairRequirement':'Evaluate fallback only for relevant text writes so the declared conditional schedule trigger is truthful.'},
